course: dictionary
lesson: 2746
title: Disagreeable: unpleasant or unfriendly
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Disagreeable» has two main meanings. It can mean unpleasant, like «a disagreeable smell». It can also mean unfriendly and bad-tempered, like «a disagreeable old man». Both meanings describe something you would not enjoy.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. In «there are moments—perhaps I should say there is a moment—when one must face disagreeable tasks», the tasks are not nice to do, so here it means unpleasant. Try your meaning in the sentence: «one must face unpleasant tasks» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Grown-ups often use «disagreeable» where we would say nasty or grumpy. It sounds a little formal or old-fashioned, so you will meet it often in classic children's books, such as Mary at the start of «The Secret Garden».
fact: «Disagreeable» means unpleasant, not nice to experience.
fact: «Disagreeable» can also mean unfriendly, bad-tempered and hard to get on with.
fact: The adverb is «disagreeably», as in «he behaved disagreeably».
fact: In classic stories, a disagreeable character is often grumpy and rude, like Mary in «The Secret Garden» at the start.
fact: In everyday speech, «disagreeable» is a slightly formal or old-fashioned way to say «nasty» or «grumpy».
exercise: «The smell from the bins was disagreeable.» What does disagreeable mean here? | *Unpleasant, not nice to experience | Very loud | Hidden under the leaves | Lovely and sweet
exercise: «The old man was disagreeable to everyone who came near his gate.» What does disagreeable mean here? | Very tall | *Unfriendly and bad-tempered | Friendly and happy to chat | Lost and confused
exercise: Sam says «disagreeable» means delightful. Who is right? | Neither word means anything at all | Both are right, they mean the same | *Sam is wrong, it means unpleasant or unfriendly | Sam is right, it means lovely
test: In «a disagreeable smell», what does disagreeable tell you about the smell? | Pleasant | *Unpleasant | Invisible | Sweet
test: Which sentence uses disagreeable to mean grumpy and unfriendly? | «The disagreeable bus arrived right on time.» | *«The disagreeable waiter scowled at us and never smiled.» | «The disagreeable cake was warm and tasty.» | «The disagreeable puppy wagged its tail all afternoon.»
exam: In «there are moments—perhaps I should say there is a moment—when one must face disagreeable tasks», what does disagreeable mean? | Sparkling and bright | Quiet and calm | *Unpleasant, not nice to do | Nice and fun
